KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--unwind 2 --unwinding-assertions
^\[[^]]*fill\.unwind\.0\] line 11 unwinding assertion loop 0: FAILURE$
^\[[^]]*fill\.unwind\.0\] line 21 unwinding assertion loop 0: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
set_properties names a loop's unwinding property after the function's base
name; a::fill and b::fill both got `fill.unwind.0', and only one result
(line 11) was reported.  Each loop needs a distinct property id.
